  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Seventh Global Environment Facility Replenishment - Core Contribution - Environmental Challenges</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Global Environment Facility (GEF) was established in 1992 and is a multilateral family of funds dedicated to addressing climate change, biodiversity loss, pollution, and supporting land and ocean health. Through the GEF, Australia meets its financial obligations under numerous multilateral environmental agreements to support developing countries address environmental challenges, including the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change, United Nations Convention on Biological Diversity, United Nations Convention to Combat Desertification, Stockholm Convention on Persistent Organic Pollutants and Minamata Convention on Mercury. This funding (total value: $76.67 million) represents Australia&apos;s contribution to the GEF&apos;s seventh replenishment (2018-22). Funding is provided to the GEF Trust Fund with the World Bank as trustee.</narrative>
  </description>
